Package: sqlr
Title: Represent and Generate SQL Schemas
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Nicolas", "Bennett", email = "r@nbenn.ch", role = c("aut", "cre")))
Description:
    A dialect-independent representation of a relational schema -- tables,
    columns, types, constraints and indexes -- that can be built up from R,
    rendered as data definition language for a given SQL dialect, and learned
    back from a live database. Dialect support is provided by companion
    packages.
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
    S7,
    utils
Suggests:
    DBI,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
URL: https://github.com/nbenn/sqlr
BugReports: https://github.com/nbenn/sqlr/issues
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.0
